# ✅ **Your VirtualBox is installed from pacman (official Arch/Manjaro repo)**

Because the `Repository` line says:

```
Repository      : extra
```

and the packager is an Arch maintainer:

```
Packager : Christian Hesse <eworm@archlinux.org>
```

So **you are using official repo VirtualBox, NOT AUR**.
This is good — more stable and supports Guest Additions properly.

---

# ✅ **Next Step: Install the Guest Additions ISO (you don’t have it yet)**

Your output also shows:

```
Optional Deps: virtualbox-guest-iso: Guest Additions CD image
```

➡️ This means the ISO is **not installed**.

Install it using:

```bash
sudo pacman -S virtualbox-guest-iso
```

This will put the ISO here:

```
/usr/lib/virtualbox/additions/VBoxGuestAdditions.iso
```

---

# ✅ **Then mount inside VM**

In VirtualBox menu (VM running):

```
Devices → Optical Drives → Choose Disk File…
```

Select:

```
/usr/lib/virtualbox/additions/VBoxGuestAdditions.iso
```

Inside Windows 11 VM, run:

```
VBoxWindowsAdditions.exe
```

Reboot VM afterwards.

---

